public virtual int Add(Object value)
{
    if (_size == _items.Length) EnsureCapacity(_size + 1);
    _items[_size] = value;
    _version++;

    return _size++;
}
```

In the function `Add`, when an element is added, the size of the list (`_size`) is first increased by 1, and then the added element is assigned to the new position `_size`. The return value of the function is the index of the added element which is `_size - 1`. So the assert statement checks if the return value (`RET`) is within the valid range defined by `MaxArrayLength`.
